  "answer_text": "The standard, most widely accepted pronunciation for the meme and the cryptocurrency (Dogecoin) is **\"dohj\"** (phonetically written as **/do\u028ad\u0292/**). \n\nA breakdown of how to pronounce it, why it\u2019s pronounced that way, and a few common variations:\n\n### 1. The Standard Pronunciation: \"Dohj\"\nThis is the pronunciation recognized by dictionaries, major news outlets, and Jackson Palmer (the co-creator of Dogecoin).\n* **How it sounds:** It rhymes with **\"vogue\"**, but ends with a soft **\"j\"** sound (like in \"judge\" or \"jury\"). \n* **Another way to think of it:** Say the word **\"dough\"** (as in cookie dough), and add a **\"j\"** sound to the end: **\"dough-j.\"**\n\n### 2. The Original French-Style Variation: \"Dohzh\"\nSome people pronounce it as **/do\u028a\u0292/**, ending with a soft, French-sounding \"zh\". \n* **How it sounds:** This rhymes with the word **\"beige\"** or **\"prestige.\"**\n* **Why it exists:** The very first time the word \"doge\" was used as a misspelled slang for \"dog\" was in a 2005 episode of the puppet show *Homestar Runner*. In the episode, the character Homestar spells out \"D-O-G-E\" to Strong Bad and pronounces it **\"dohzh\"**. Because of this, many internet purists consider \"dohzh\" to be the most authentic pronunciation.\n\n### Common Mispronunciations (What *not* to say)\nBecause \"doge\" is an internet-coined word, people have guessed many different pronunciations over the years. You will often hear people incorrectly say:\n* **\"Dohg\"** (Rhyming with *rogue* or *vogue* with a hard \"g\" sound).\n* **\"Dog-ee\"** (Pronounced exactly like *doggy*).\n* **\"Dodge\"** (Rhyming with *lodge*, using a short \"o\" sound).\n\n### Bonus Fact: The Historical \"Doge\"\nIf you are referring to the historical **Doge of Venice** (the chief magistrate of the former Republic of Venice), it is also pronounced **\"dohj\"**. If you stick to **\"dohj\"** (dough-j), you will be correct in both historical and internet contexts!",
